\subsection{Centring through run contrasts}
\label{app:centring}
The raw cross-half products contain squared configuration means. The analysis record reports that these squared means can inflate the ratio by roughly three orders of magnitude. The described implementation projects scores onto an orthonormal basis of mean-zero run contrasts. Each basis row annihilates the all-ones vector, making raw and centred inputs equivalent under projection. Our runtime checks test row sums and invariance of $\sum_c T_c$ under a shared configuration shift on both halves, addressing centring errors without testing measurement or exchangeability assumptions.

